जिज्ञासुरपि योगस्य शब्दब्रह्मातिवर्तते ॥ ४४ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2044,\"bb\":1808,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/44/b1808/\",\"body_value\":\"pūrvābhyāsena tenaiva
hriyate hy avaśo ’pi saḥ
jijñāsur api yogasya
śabda-brahmātivartate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2045,\"bb\":1809,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/44/b1809/\",\"shadow_value\":\"pūrva – previous; abhyāsena – by practice; tena – by that; eva – certainly; hriyate – is attracted; hi – surely; avaśaḥ – automatically; api – also; saḥ – he; jijñāsuḥ – inquisitive; api – even; yogasya – about yoga; śabda-brahma – ritualistic principles of scriptures; ativartate – transcends.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"pūrva\",\"translation\":\"previous\"},{\"word\":\"abhyāsena\",\"translation\":\"by practice\"},{\"word\":\"tena\",\"translation\":\"by that\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"hriyate\",\"translation\":\"is attracted\"},{\"word\":\"hi\",\"translation\":\"surely\"},{\"word\":\"avaśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"automatically\"},{\"word\":\"api\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"},{\"word\":\"jijñāsuḥ\",\"translation\":\"inquisitive\"},{\"word\":\"api\",\"translation\":\"even\"},{\"word\":\"yogasya\",\"translation\":\"about yoga\"},{\"word\":\"śabda-brahma\",\"translation\":\"ritualistic principles of scriptures\"},{\"word\":\"ativartate\",\"translation\":\"transcends\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2046,\"bb\":1810,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/44/b1810/\",\"body_value\":\"By virtue of the divine consciousness of his previous life, he automatically becomes attracted to the yogic principles – even without seeking them. Such an inquisitive transcendentalist stands always above the ritualistic principles of the scriptures.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2047,\"bb\":1811,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/44/b1811/\",\"body_value\":\"Advanced yogīs are not very much attracted to the rituals of the scriptures, but they automatically become attracted to the yoga principles, which can elevate them to complete Kṛṣṇa consciousness, the highest yoga perfection. In the Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam (3.33.7), such disregard of Vedic rituals by the advanced transcendentalists is explained as follows:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2048,\"bb\":1812,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/44/b1812/\",\"body_value\":\"aho bata śva-paco ’to garīyān
yaj-jihvāgre vartate nāma tubhyam
